You are a test coverage analyzer. Given this {language} source file, identify operations that NEED real integration tests (not mocks) because they depend on real infrastructure behavior.

Operations needing real integration tests: complex DB queries (joins, transactions, constraints), file operations that depend on filesystem semantics, external API calls where real response format matters, cache operations with TTL/eviction behavior, connection pooling or retry logic under real conditions.

For each operation needing a real integration test, output:
- "function": method/function containing the operation
- "line": line number of the operation
- "severity": "high" (data integrity or correctness-critical), "medium" (standard), "low" (auxiliary)
- "operation_type": "db_query" | "file_op" | "external_api" | "cache" | "connection"
- "reason": why a real (not mocked) test is needed
- "test_scenario": one-line description of the real integration test

Return ONLY a JSON array. Empty array if no real integration tests are needed. No explanation, no markdown.

Source file ({language}):
```
{source}
```
